{
  "_doc": "Audio mix (0.107, src/audio/): clip trims (gainDb) bring every sound effect to an intended loudness (measuredDb = the file's loudest 50ms, measured in 0.107; measuredDb + gainDb = hits sit around -12 dB, rare finds and stingers louder, the click subtle). Buses: music and effects -> master -> limiter (a safety net: louder rare finds, sliders, stacked hits). sfxLevel 0.7 keeps the overall level where 0.106 was. voices: at most maxPerClip copies of one clip and maxTotal overall, repeats within retriggerMs dropped, each copy already sounding lowers the next by stackDb. pan.width = how far left/right sounds sit (0 = mono, 1 = hard). duck = the music dips by db under these stingers for the given seconds. volumes = default slider positions (0-1; players' own settings persist in localStorage). music.tracks (0.114; every bed an ElevenLabs score since 0.00282, cut from its take by tools/gen-score.mjs --import at the loop seam it finds) = per scene the bed: a loop of loopS seconds with tailS seconds more of the music's own continuation past it, crossfade 'power' (the tail and the start are different passages, so they sum by power — audio/musicLoop.js), gainDb its level trim (the import levels a take to the bed it replaces; 0.114 set the first trims to match the old beds as played, in Chromium). The procedural beds before them were exact loops with their first tailS seconds appended, crossfaded at equal gain — a track without `crossfade` still gets that. 0.108: victory (then the run end's 'You escaped!' fanfare; since 0.162 only the win dialog's chime, ui/victoryModal.js) 30% quieter (-3.1 dB); whoosh = the generated room-to-room sound (audio/synth.js), measured from an offline render. 0.110: variation = per-hit variety for the strikes: a random pitch (rate), a random tone colour (a peaking EQ between eq.lo and eq.hi Hz, +/- eq.db) and random articulation layers generated in audio/synth.js (tick = blade glint, thud = body, slice = the swing's air, clank = armour), each joining with probability p at db (layer trims put them 6-12 dB under the hit: tick raw -17.1, thud -11.7, slice -23.5, clank -13.9 dB). loot (the coin jingle) 3 dB quieter. 0.118: clips is the one sound registry — per name a file (or synth: generated by audio/synth.js, trim 0 = the caller sets the level), gainDb, stinger (never cut off for another sound), rate [lo, hi] + jitterDb (random pitch / level per play; a variation config below overrides the pitch). Every class clip (atk_ / heavy_ / hurt_<id>) has a variation entry of its own, and where one exists its rate is the pitch played — clips.<x>.rate is then the fallback for a play with no variation (sfx.js). 0.161: narration = the Old Wizard voice-over (audio/narrator.js; the takes are assets/data/narration.json, generated): every take is levelled so its loudest 50 ms lands at targetDb (just over the hits at -12); gapS = silence kept between two lines, maxWaitS = a line that would have to wait longer than this for the one playing is dropped; roomEntryDelayMs / combatDelayMs = how long after a room entry / a combat line prints its narration starts. lines = when a line plays: chance per event (1 = every time), firstInRoom (the first time in a room it always plays, then chance), oncePerRoom / oncePerRun / oncePerSession, cooldownMs (not again within). Once-per-save lines (victory, first_death) are gated by the code that fires them. 0.173: transition = the room change's sound, played so the clip's loudest 50 ms (clips.<clip>.peakMs, measured) lands peakAtMs into the transition — the middle of windows out (1 s) + crossfade (2 s) + windows in (1 s). 0.00297: clips lists the developer's ten whoosh recordings (whoosh_long_1-3, whoosh_grainy_1-4, whoosh_fly_1-3 in assets/audio/sfx), one picked at random each change and timed by its own peakMs, all levelled at the hits' -12 dB (measuredDb + gainDb; 0.00298 — at the old swoosh's -19.3 they were way too quiet, the developer found), jitterDb varying the level; the one pitched-down swoosh (sfx-room-swoosh-v2.mp3, 0.175-0.178) and its variation entry are gone. The generated whoosh went in 0.173. The swoosh file clip is the dodge (combatQueue.js). 0.00297 too: death = the developer's huge wooden tube (death_v2.mp3), a stinger whose peakMs times it to the YOU DIED dialog (dungeonScene.js sfxPeakAt); revive = the developer's spooky metal hit, a stinger under duck.clips like the shrine, played when the Heart revives the knight (combatQueue.js) or the reliquary's price is paid back by it (treasureUI.js); loot (the coin jingle) plays an octave down (rate 0.44-0.56; it read too high). 0.00298: deeper = the developer's huge tom, struck as the player chooses Push Deeper (dungeonScene.js nextRoom) or the hall's Descend begins (hubScene.js enterDungeon), at the hits' -12 dB. 0.00287: cries = the get-hit recordings, pulled for now (the developer's call: the content wants more thought) — hero false = a blow on the hero plays the plain hurt, not hurt_<class>; foe false = a struck foe makes no ehurt_<id> cry (its eatk_ attack stays). The clips stay registered; flip to true to hear them again.",
