  "_classSfx": "The classes' and the foes' sounds (0.00270; recordings since 0.00271): atk_<id> / heavy_<id> / hurt_<id> per hero (combatQueue.js sfxFor picks them by the save's class) and eatk_<id> / ehurt_<id> per foe (combatSfx.js: the struck foe's cry with the hero's blow, the striking foe's attack with the hero's hurt) are rendered recordings — tools/gen-sfx.mjs sends docs/sfx-prompts.md's line per clip through ElevenLabs' sound generation into assets/audio/sfx/<clip>_v1.mp3 (a new name per take, rule 7: --redo gives _v2) — each measured in the browser by tools/audio-check.mjs (measuredDb; ffmpeg's 16 kHz measure under-read the hissy ones by up to 4 dB) and trimmed by gainDb so a hero's blow and hurt land at -12 dB like the hits, a heavy at -10, a foe's own sound at -14 under the hero's. The class's variation entry rides on top as its colour: the pitch (rate) and the synth layers from audio/synth.js (swing, crackle, zap, wail, rake, chime, hiss, grunt — the grunt's layerRate is the class's voice). A possible doubled voice to listen for: the hurt recordings carry each class's own cry and the grunt layer still plays under them — a listen decides whether the grunt goes. 0.00277: the grunt layer came off every hurt_ clip (the recordings carry each class's cry; the two doubled)."
